IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 16 -- Wrongful restraint, wrongful confinement, criminal force and assault`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 339, 340, 345, 346, 347, 348, 349, 350, 351, 353, 354, 354A,
-- 355, 356, 357, 358.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Two of the Act's sub-headings, kept in one module because they interlock: s 354A
-- aggravates outraging modesty by causing wrongful restraint, and s 357 is an
-- assault committed in attempting wrongful confinement. Splitting them would put a
-- cycle between the two files.
--
-- Shape of the group. s 339 defines wrongful restraint; s 340 makes wrongful
-- confinement a species of it; ss 345 to 348 aggravate confinement by a
-- circumstance or a purpose. s 349 defines force with no fault element at all;
-- s 350 adds the fault and makes it criminal force; s 351 makes the apprehension of
-- criminal force an assault; ss 353 to 357 aggravate the assault or criminal force.
-- ss 352 and 358 are the mitigated and unmitigated provocation cases.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. ss 341, 342 and 352 are punishment sections. Several
-- sections here state a minimum or a term "in addition to" another; none of that is
-- encoded. ss 352 and 358 are encoded for their provocation test, which is a real
-- element, not for the terms they prescribe.

§§ `Section 339 -- Wrongful restraint`

-- Whoever voluntarily obstructs any person so as to prevent that person from
-- proceeding in any direction in which that person has a right to proceed is said
-- wrongfully to restrain that person.
--
-- Exception: the obstruction of a private way over land or water which a person in
-- good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct is not an offence
-- within the meaning of this section. This is an exception written into the section
-- itself, so unlike the Chapter 4 exceptions it is a negated conjunct here rather
-- than something applied by the wrapper.
-- Illustration: A obstructs a path Z has a right to pass along, A not believing in
-- good faith that he has a right to stop it. A wrongfully restrains Z.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 339"
@export Decide whether a person is wrongfully restrained within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 339
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Voluntary obstruction preventing a person from proceeding in a direction in which that person has a right to proceed, and whether the section's own private-way exception applies.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is wrongfully restrained` IF
        l's `voluntarily obstructs any person so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction in which that person has a right to proceed`
    AND (NOT l's `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which the accused in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct`)

§§ `Section 340 -- Wrongful confinement`

-- Whoever wrongfully restrains any person in such a manner as to prevent that person
-- from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits is said wrongfully to confine
-- that person. Confinement is therefore restraint plus the circumscribing limits,
-- and every wrongful confinement is also a wrongful restraint.
-- Illustration (b): placing armed men at the outlets of a building and telling Z
-- they will fire if Z leaves is wrongful confinement, though no wall encloses Z.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 340"
@export Decide whether a person is wrongfully confined within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 340
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Wrongful restraint under s 339, in such a manner as to prevent the person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is wrongfully confined` IF
        `the person is wrongfully restrained` l
    AND l's `the restraint prevents that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits`

§§ `Sections 345 to 348 -- Aggravated wrongful confinement`

-- s 345: keeping a person in wrongful confinement knowing that a writ for that
-- person's liberation has been duly issued.
-- s 346: confining in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the
-- confinement, or the place of it, may not be known to or discovered by any person
-- interested in the person confined or any public servant.
-- s 347: confining for the purpose of extorting property or a valuable security, or
-- of constraining to do anything illegal or to give information which may facilitate
-- an offence.
-- s 348: confining for the purpose of extorting a confession or information leading
-- to the detection of an offence or misconduct, or of compelling restoration of
-- property, satisfaction of a claim, or information leading to restoration.
--
-- ss 347 and 348 are close neighbours of ss 327 and 330 in the hurt group, but the
-- wording is not identical -- s 347 says "to do anything illegal or to give any
-- information which may facilitate the commission of an offence" where s 327 says
-- "to do anything which is illegal or which may facilitate the commission of an
-- offence". The facts are kept separate rather than shared, so that neither section
-- is read through the other's words.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 345"
@export Decide whether the confinement is of a person for whose liberation a writ has been issued under Penal Code 1871 section 345
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Wrongful confinement kept up with knowledge that a writ for the person's liberation has been duly issued.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes wrongful confinement despite a writ of liberation` IF
        `the person is wrongfully confined` l
    AND l's `keeps the person in wrongful confinement knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 346"
@export Decide whether the confinement is a wrongful confinement in secret under Penal Code 1871 section 346
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Wrongful confinement in a manner indicating an intention that it, or its place, be concealed from anyone interested in the person confined or from a public servant.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes wrongful confinement in secret` IF
        `the person is wrongfully confined` l
    AND l's `confines in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement or the place of it may not be known to or discovered by any person interested in the person confined or any public servant`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 347"
@export Decide whether the confinement is for the purpose of extorting property or constraining to an illegal act under Penal Code 1871 section 347
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Wrongful confinement for either of the two purposes in s 347.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes wrongful confinement to extort property or constrain to an illegal act` IF
        `the person is wrongfully confined` l
    AND (   l's `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined or from any person interested in him any property or valuable security`
         OR l's `for the purpose of constraining the person confined or any person interested in him to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 348"
@export Decide whether the confinement is for the purpose of extorting a confession or compelling restoration of property under Penal Code 1871 section 348
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Wrongful confinement for either of the two purposes in s 348.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes wrongful confinement to extort a confession` IF
        `the person is wrongfully confined` l
    AND (   l's `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined or from any person interested in him any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`
         OR l's `for the purpose of constraining the person confined or any person interested in him to restore or to cause the restoration of any property or valuable security or to satisfy any claim or demand or to give information which may lead to such restoration`)

§§ `Section 349 -- Force`

-- A person uses force to another if he causes motion, change of motion or cessation
-- of motion to that other, or causes to any substance such motion as brings that
-- substance into contact with any part of that other's body, with anything that
-- other is wearing or carrying, or with anything so situated that such contact
-- affects that other's sense of feeling.
--
-- The proviso is a closed list of three ways -- own bodily power, disposing a
-- substance so the motion follows without further act, or inducing an animal -- and
-- is a requirement, not a gloss: force is used only if the motion was caused in one
-- of those ways. So the rule is a disjunction of the two effects conjoined with a
-- disjunction of the three ways.
-- s 349 carries no fault element at all. It is a physical description, and on its
-- own describes no offence.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 349"
@export Decide whether force is used to another within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 349
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Motion, change of motion or cessation of motion caused to a person or to a substance brought into contact with them, by one of the three ways in the proviso.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `force is used to another` IF
        (   l's `causes motion change of motion or cessation of motion to that other`
         OR l's `causes to any substance such motion change of motion or cessation of motion as brings that substance into contact with any part of that other body or with anything that other is wearing or carrying or with anything so situated that such contact affects that other sense of feeling`)
    AND (   l's `by his own bodily power`
         OR l's `by disposing any substance in such a manner that the motion or change or cessation of motion takes place without any further act on his part or on the part of any other person`
         OR l's `by inducing any animal to move to change its motion or to cease to move`)

§§ `Section 350 -- Criminal force`

-- Whoever intentionally uses force to any person, without that person's consent, in
-- order to cause the committing of any offence, or intending by the use of such
-- force illegally to cause, or knowing it to be likely that by the use of such force
-- he will illegally cause, injury, fear or annoyance to the person to whom the force
-- is used.
--
-- Three elements: the intentional use of s 349 force, the absence of consent, and
-- one of three purposes or states of mind. Illustrations (a) to (h) each turn on the
-- last: the same physical act is force simpliciter or criminal force according to
-- what the actor meant by it.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 350"
@export Decide whether criminal force is used within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 350
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Intentional use of s 349 force without consent, in order to cause an offence to be committed, or intending or knowing it likely that injury, fear or annoyance will illegally be caused.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `criminal force is used` IF
        `force is used to another` l
    AND l's `intentionally uses force to any person`
    AND l's `without that person consent`
    AND (   l's `in order to cause the committing of any offence`
         OR l's `intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury fear or annoyance to the person to whom the force is used`
         OR l's `knowing it to be likely that by the use of such force he will illegally cause injury fear or annoyance to that person`)

§§ `Section 351 -- Assault`

-- Whoever makes any gesture or any preparation, intending or knowing it to be likely
-- that such gesture or preparation will cause any person present to apprehend that
-- he who makes it is about to use criminal force to that person, is said to commit
-- an assault.
--
-- Explanation: mere words do not amount to an assault, but the words a person uses
-- may give his gestures or preparations such a meaning as makes them amount to one.
-- The first half is a limit and is encoded as a negated conjunct; the second half is
-- why the limit is narrow -- it excludes only the case resting on words with no
-- gesture or preparation at all, which is what Illustration (c) turns on.
-- Note that an assault needs no force to be used, and no contact: it is complete on
-- the apprehension.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 351"
@export Decide whether an assault is committed within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 351
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc A gesture or preparation, made intending or knowing it likely to cause a person present to apprehend that criminal force is about to be used. Words alone are not enough, though words may give a gesture its meaning.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an assault is committed` IF
        l's `makes any gesture or any preparation`
    AND l's `intending or knowing it to be likely that such gesture or preparation will cause any person present to apprehend that he is about to use criminal force to that person`
    AND (NOT l's `the case rests on words alone unaccompanied by any gesture or preparation`)

§§ `Assault or criminal force -- the common opening of sections 352 to 358`

-- Every section from s 352 to s 358 opens "Whoever assaults or uses criminal force
-- to any person". That disjunction is gathered once here.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 350 and 351"
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person assaults or uses criminal force` IF
        `an assault is committed` l
    OR  `criminal force is used` l

§§ `Sections 352 and 358 -- Grave and sudden provocation`

-- s 352 punishes assault or criminal force "otherwise than on grave and sudden
-- provocation given by that person"; s 358 punishes the same on such provocation,
-- far more lightly. The two are complementary, and the provocation fact is a real
-- element of each rather than a sentencing factor.
--
-- The Explanation to s 352 -- which ss 355 and 358 adopt -- names three cases in
-- which grave and sudden provocation will NOT mitigate: where the provocation was
-- sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse; where the offender
-- knows or has reason to believe it was given by something done in obedience to the
-- law or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers; and where it was
-- given by something done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence.
-- All three are encoded as disqualifiers of the provocation, so that a disqualified
-- provocation leaves the case in s 352 rather than s 358.
-- "Whether the provocation was grave and sudden enough to mitigate the offence is a
-- question of fact" -- so the first fact below is the court's conclusion, asserted.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 352 Explanation"
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provocation mitigates` IF
        l's `on grave and sudden provocation given by that person`
    AND (NOT l's `the provocation was sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for the offence`)
    AND (NOT l's `the offender knows or has reason to believe that the provocation is given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of the powers of such public servant`)
    AND (NOT l's `the provocation is given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 352"
@export Decide whether the case is one of assault or criminal force otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation under Penal Code 1871 section 352
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Assault or criminal force where no mitigating grave and sudden provocation was given by the person assaulted.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes assault or criminal force otherwise than on provocation` IF
        `the person assaults or uses criminal force` l
    AND (NOT `the provocation mitigates` l)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 358"
@export Decide whether the case is one of assault or criminal force on grave and sudden provocation under Penal Code 1871 section 358
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Assault or criminal force on grave and sudden provocation given by the person assaulted, the provocation not being disqualified by the s 352 Explanation.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes assault or criminal force on provocation` IF
        `the person assaults or uses criminal force` l
    AND `the provocation mitigates` l

§§ `Section 353 -- To deter a public servant from the discharge of his duty`

-- Assault or criminal force to a person being a public servant in the execution of
-- his duty as such; or with intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging
-- his duty; or in consequence of anything done or attempted in the lawful discharge
-- of it. The three limbs mirror ss 332 and 333 in the hurt group, except that s 353
-- does not extend the deterrence limb to "any other public servant".

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 353"
@export Decide whether criminal force is used to deter a public servant from the discharge of his duty under Penal Code 1871 section 353
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Assault or criminal force on one of the three public-servant limbs of s 353.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes using criminal force to deter a public servant` IF
        `the person assaults or uses criminal force` l
    AND (   l's `the person assaulted is a public servant in the execution of his duty as such public servant`
         OR l's `with intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging his duty as such public servant`
         OR l's `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant`)

§§ `Sections 354 and 354A -- Outraging modesty`

-- s 354(1): assault or criminal force to any person, intending to outrage or knowing
-- it to be likely that the modesty of that person will thereby be outraged.
-- s 354(2) raises the maximum where the person is below 14. That is punishment, and
-- the age fact is carried for the caller rather than as an element of s 354(1).
--
-- s 354A(1): voluntarily causing or attempting to cause death, hurt, wrongful
-- restraint, or fear of instant death, instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint, in
-- order to commit or facilitate an offence under s 354. Note that s 354A does not
-- require the s 354 offence to have been committed -- the purpose is enough.
-- s 354A(2) raises the minimum where the offence is committed in a lift or against a
-- person below 14. Punishment again; both facts are carried, neither is an element.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 354(1)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes assault or criminal force with intent to outrage modesty under Penal Code 1871 section 354
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Assault or criminal force, with intent to outrage modesty or knowledge that it is likely to be outraged.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes outraging modesty` IF
        `the person assaults or uses criminal force` l
    AND l's `intending to outrage or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty of that person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 354A(1)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes outraging modesty in the aggravated circumstances of Penal Code 1871 section 354A
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Voluntarily causing or attempting to cause death, hurt, wrongful restraint or fear of instant death, hurt or restraint, in order to commit or facilitate a s 354 offence. The s 354 offence need not have been committed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes outraging modesty in aggravated circumstances` IF
        l's `in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence under section 354`
    AND l's `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person death or hurt or wrongful restraint or fear of instant death instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint`

§§ `Sections 355 to 357 -- The remaining aggravated assaults`

-- s 355: assault or criminal force intending thereby to dishonour the person,
-- otherwise than on grave and sudden provocation given by that person. The
-- Explanation adopts the s 352 Explanation, so the same three disqualifiers apply.
-- s 356: assault or criminal force in committing or attempting to commit theft of
-- property which the person is then wearing or carrying.
-- s 357: assault or criminal force in attempting wrongfully to confine the person.
-- Note s 357 needs only the attempt, not a completed confinement under s 340.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 355"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes assault or criminal force with intent to dishonour under Penal Code 1871 section 355
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Assault or criminal force intending to dishonour the person, where no mitigating grave and sudden provocation was given.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes assault or criminal force with intent to dishonour` IF
        `the person assaults or uses criminal force` l
    AND l's `intending thereby to dishonour that person`
    AND (NOT `the provocation mitigates` l)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 356"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes assault or criminal force in committing theft of property carried by a person under Penal Code 1871 section 356
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Assault or criminal force in committing or attempting theft of property the person is then wearing or carrying.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes assault or criminal force in committing theft from the person` IF
        `the person assaults or uses criminal force` l
    AND l's `in committing or attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then wearing or carrying`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 357"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes assault or criminal force in attempting wrongfully to confine a person under Penal Code 1871 section 357
GIVEN l IS A `Personal Liberty` @desc Assault or criminal force in attempting wrongfully to confine the person. The confinement need not be completed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes assault or criminal force in attempting wrongful confinement` IF
        `the person assaults or uses criminal force` l
    AND l's `in attempting wrongfully to confine that person`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes wrongful restraint` IF
        `the person is wrongfully restrained` (a's `personal liberty`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes wrongful confinement` IF
        `the person is wrongfully confined` (a's `personal liberty`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes assault or criminal force` IF
        `the person assaults or uses criminal force` (a's `personal liberty`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes outraging modesty` IF
        (   `constitutes outraging modesty` (a's `personal liberty`)
         OR `constitutes outraging modesty in aggravated circumstances` (a's `personal liberty`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
